                <pb facs="0727" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Brazil/5191: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-23T22:00:00-04:00">September 23, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3611. Concerning telegram being sent concurrently by OEW in answer to Embassy’s
                    4374, September 14, Department and Commodity Credit Corporation believe that it
                    would be desirable to have exchanges of brief diplomatic notes covering each of
                    the commodities rather than elaborate commercial contracts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
